        "math_academy_id": "q-129275",
        "problem": "Calculate \n${\\int }_{3}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{5}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\u27e8-4,\\,-12,\\,14\u27e9$\nand\n${\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\u27e82,\\,8,\\,-8\u27e9.$",
        "worked_solution": "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{5}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\u27e8-4,\\,-12,\\,14\u27e9-\u27e82,\\,8,\\,-8\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e84,\\,12,\\,-14\u27e9-\u27e82,\\,8,\\,-8\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e82,\\,4,\\,-6\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "actual_result": "Correct",
